        {
          "tipo": "gramatica",
          "min": 12,
          "titulo": "Este, esse, aquele: pointing at things",
          "explicacao": "STEP 1: Portuguese has three levels of distance. «Este / esta» is near the speaker; «esse / essa» is near the listener or a little farther; «aquele / aquela» is far from both. Plurals: «estes, estas; esses, essas; aqueles, aquelas». STEP 2: they agree with the noun: «esta camisa», «esse casaco», «aquelas calças». STEP 3: in everyday Brazilian speech «esse / essa» often takes the place of «este / esta», even for things in your hand: «Quanto custa esse casaco?» «Este» is common in writing, formal speech and some regions. Both are right. STEP 4: when you do not name the thing, use the neutral words «isto, isso, aquilo», which have no gender and no plural: «O que é isso?» (What is this/that?). Never put «isto / isso / aquilo» before a noun. STEP 5: after «de» and «em» they contract, as «no» and «na» did: de + esse = desse, em + esse = nesse, em + aquela = naquela. So: «a cor desse casaco», «Moro naquela rua». The words «aqui» (here), «aí» (there, near you) and «lá» or «ali» (over there) go along with the three levels.",
          "comparacao": "English has only two levels, this and that. Portuguese has three: this (near me), that (near you) and that over there (far from both). In speech, though, many Brazilians use just two, «esse» and «aquele». Also, English «this» or «that» alone can be a pronoun («What is that?»); in Portuguese the pronoun for an unnamed thing is a separate word: «isso».",
          "exemplos": [
            {
              "ru": "Esta camisa é azul.",
              "pt": "This shirt is blue."
            },
            {
              "ru": "Esse casaco é bonito.",
              "pt": "That coat is nice."
            },
            {
              "ru": "Aquelas calças pretas são caras.",
              "pt": "Those black trousers are expensive."
            },
            {
              "ru": "O que é isso?",
              "pt": "What is this?"
            },
            {
              "ru": "Eu moro naquela rua.",
              "pt": "I live on that street."
            },
            {
              "ru": "A cor desse vestido é rosa.",
              "pt": "The color of that dress is pink."
            }
          ],
