          "tipo": "gramatica",
          "min": 8,
          "titulo": "Prices above 100, sizes and paying",
          "explicacao": "STEP 1: to ask a price, use «Quanto custa?» for one item and «Quanto custam?» for several. In speech «Quanto é?» and «Quanto está?» are also common. STEP 2: hundreds: 100 is «cem» when it is alone and «cento» in front of other numbers: «cento e vinte». Then «duzentos, trezentos, quatrocentos, quinhentos, seiscentos, setecentos, oitocentos, novecentos», and 1,000 is «mil». With feminine nouns the hundreds change: «duzentas camisas». STEP 3: prices use a comma for the decimals and «R$» before the number: R$ 89,90 is read «oitenta e nove reais e noventa centavos», or in speech simply «oitenta e nove e noventa». STEP 4: sizes. For clothes say «Eu uso M» or «Meu tamanho é M» (the sizes are P, M, G, GG). For shoes the size is a number: «Eu calço 38» is also said. Useful questions: «Posso experimentar?», «Onde fica o provador?», «Tem o P?». STEP 5: to decide, say «Vou levar» (I'll take it). It is a fixed phrase for now. You study the structure «ir + infinitive» in lesson 17. To pay: «no cartão» (by card) or «em dinheiro» (in cash). In Brazil it is common to ask for the payment in installments on the card, and many shops accept Pix, an instant payment through the phone.",
